text: >-
  References & Methodology

  followtheepicenter.com

  METHODOLOGY

  Ratings reflect how directly each hypothesis predicts or explains each finding
  without

  requiring additional assumptions or secondary mechanisms.

  5 = Finding is a direct, first-principles prediction of the hypothesis

  4 = Finding is strongly consistent with the hypothesis

  3 = Finding is possible under the hypothesis / neither supports nor
  contradicts

  2 = Finding requires secondary mechanisms or additional assumptions

  1 = Finding is difficult or impossible to explain under the hypothesis

  0 = Mechanism does not apply to this hypothesis

  BLAST INJURY LITERATURE

  [1] Cooper GJ, Townend DJ, Cater SR, et al.

  'The role of stress waves in thoracic visceral

  injury from blast loading.' J Biomech 1991; 24:273-284.

  [2]

  Cooper GJ.

  'Protection of the lung from blast overpressures by thoracic stress wave

  decouplers.' J Trauma 1996; 40(Suppl): S105-S110.

  Courtney AC, Courtney MW.

  blast pressure waves.

  • Med Ayotreses 20c9; 12: of mild traumatic brain injury due to

  Courtney MW, Courtney AC.

  'Working toward exposure thresholds for blast-induced

  traumatic brain injury. Neurolmage 2011; 54(S1): S55-S61.

  Cernak I, et al. 'Exposure of the thorax to a sublethal blast wave causes a

  hydrodynamic pulse that leads to perivenular inflammation in the brain.'

  J Neurotrauma 2014; 31:1292-1304.

  D'yachenko AI, Manyuhina OV.

  'Modeling of weak blast wave propagation in the lung.'

  J Biomech 2006; 39:2113-2122.

  RESPIRATORY PHYSIOLOGY

  Hopkins E, Sharma S. 'Physiology, Functional Residual Capacity. StatPearls
  2022.

  FRC in normal adult male approx.

  3.0 L (2.5-3.5 L range).

  Breatnach E, Abbott GC, Fraser RG. 'Dimensions of the normal human trachea.'

  AJR Am J Roentgenol 1984; 142(5):903-906.

  Cinar U, et al.

  'Tracheal length in adult human: 100 autopsies.'

  Int J Morphol 2016; 34(1): 232-236.

  THORACIC RESONANCE

  [10] CT-FEM of the human thorax. Comput Methods Programs Biomed 2024.

  Resonance frequencies at 28 Hz and 41 Hz

  (structural modes).

  [11] Goodwin MJ. 'Measurement of Resonant Frequencies in the Human Chest.'

  Proc Inst Mech Eng [H] 1994. Males: 25 Hz, Females: 33 Hz.

  [12] McKusick VA, et al. 'The acoustic basis of chest examination.'

  Am Rev Tuberc 1955; 72:12-34. First resonant freq: ~125 Hz (males).

  [13] DuBois AB, et al. 'Oscillation mechanics of lungs and chest in man.'

  J Appl Physiol 1956; 8(6):587-594.

  ACOUSTIC DATA SOURCES

  [14] Canon XA55 (Video 15): 4-channel 48 kHz/16-bit PCM.

  GPS: 40 deg 16'39.24"N 111 deg 42'48.55"W

  15] IMG_6368, 13.mp4, 2. MOV, 1.mp4, Video2_1, 7.mp4:

  Cell phone recordings at 1x-4x audio sample rates.

  [16] Analysis window: +30 ms to +200 ms post-event onset.

  Rise time measurement: 104 microseconds (Canon XA55).

  Forensic Hypothesis Comparison | followtheepicenter.com

  State of Utah v. Tyler Robinson
